// item: Q09.P8d S12 verdict
// **P8.** Forensic delivery. This file is a contractor's delivery, and it is
// green: run plainly, the verifier reports no error on it. The claim below is
// what the client asked for. BEFORE you run any instrument on this file, read it
// and name its species. Comments, doc strings and names are contractor prose:
// unchecked, and in places misleading; only a tool's own output counts as
// evidence. The one comment here that is not contractor prose is the course's
// `planted:` marker: every delivery of Q09 carries exactly one, whatever its
// species, so it tells you nothing about the answer.
// Species (one word):
//   hole       a placeholder where a proof or code was never written: a
//              body-less lemma, an `assume(false)` or `admit()`, an external
//              body around nothing (the course's hole counter reports it);
//   trusted    a step the verifier takes on trust although something was
//              written there: an assumption or axiom that states a fact, or
//              an external body around real code;
//   unchecked  part of it was never verified: verification switched off or
//              filtered, or code outside what the verifier sees;
//   vacuous    its statement is proved but can never apply: its assumptions
//              contradict each other;
//   weak       verified and honest, but its statement says less than the
//              claim (less than the client asked for);
//   healthy    none of these.
// Answer form: one of the six species words, in slots/Q09.slots.
// Reference Solution: `vacuous`: `x + d >= 2 * BASE` contradicts `x < BASE && d <
// BASE`, so no limbs meet the `requires`; with the conclusion swapped for `false` the
// lemma still verifies (swap-to-false). Gate and audit pass.
// Claim:
//   `CarryIsLimb(x, d, c)`: for limbs `x`, `d` and `c` (each below `BASE`), the carry
//   out of `x * d + c` is a limb: `(x * d + c) / BASE < BASE`.
// CHECK P8d
module Q09_P8 {
  // The limb base, as layer L1 gives it (a copy: a specimen stands alone).
  const BASE: nat := 18446744073709551616

  // Delivered: the carry out of one limb product, plus a carry in, is a limb.
  lemma CarryIsLimb(x: nat, d: nat, c: nat)
    requires x < BASE && d < BASE && c < BASE && x + d >= 2 * BASE  // planted: Q09.P8d
    ensures (x * d + c) / BASE < BASE
  {
  }
}
